            "review_title": "Review at Hareya",
            "review_text": "Claire D\nWeybridge, England, United Kingdom23 contributions\n0\nAmazing Japanese food, just be prepared for a language barrier if you're English!\nApr 2017 • Solo\nLike a typical awful tourist, I speak almost no Vietnamese. This restaurant is actually wholly Japanese in that they speak Japanese to patrons, but I didn't realise this at first because they were all doing their absolute best to cater to my English needs! The English menu is quite difficult to follow, because the translations are over-simplified - I had \"soy noodle\" which turned out to be an amazing pork ramen, and \"deep fried chicken\" which was chicken on a skewer, fried in katsu style batter with hoi sin. I didn't specifically order these but because of the language barrier just asked for something good - and they did very well! The food was absolutely fantastic, they tried their absolute best to translate for me, and the service was great. And the bill came to just 130,000 dong (about £5). I speak a tiny bit of Japanese so absolutely intend to go back and use that instead!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 7, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-05",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
