            "review_text": "Karno N\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam385 contributions\n0\nCool and Different\nJan 2016 • Business\nThis is not a typical sushi restaurant but instead it is a authentic condiments Japanese restaurant that you would find in Shinjuku alleys! Yes, it is.\n\nIt was my first visit here and I was awed due to the menu because my preconceived idea had thrown me off guard completely ! \n\nThe only things close to sushi or sashimi was octopus sashimi and everything else were marinated, cooked and fermented. It was cool and nice. And the cool thing is that this place used to be a house or a hotel. So the private room has it's own WC! That's handy during a long dinner or lunch. It was business dinner for me.\n\nThe foods were nice and there are a few adventurous variety such as chicken hearts etcetera if you dare. Overall it was a pleasant experience for the men after a long working week.\n\nThe price’s are cheap. I was with 3 others and we stayed for 4 hours and the bill tally was less then $100usd.\n\nBy thw way, the owner is always there to greet you. Cool guy ! \n\nWell, enjoy and apologies for no pictures.\nRead more\nWritten January 14, 2016",
